From b4def451a8e049cf09fd14b8f1df46051267c002 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: conda-forge <conda-forge@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 08:59:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] M68K: fix off-by-one in M68K_insn_name bounds check

The CVE-2026-49282 backport in 5.0.9 checks id > ARR_SIZE(...), which
still allows reading one element past the end of s_instruction_names
when id == ARR_SIZE(...).
---
 arch/M68K/M68KInstPrinter.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/M68K/M68KInstPrinter.c b/arch/M68K/M68KInstPrinter.c
index 061edb3..721c363 100644
--- a/arch/M68K/M68KInstPrinter.c
+++ b/arch/M68K/M68KInstPrinter.c
@@ -362,7 +362,7 @@ const char* M68K_insn_name(csh handle, unsigned int id)
 #ifdef CAPSTONE_DIET
 	return NULL;
 #else
-	if (id > ARR_SIZE(s_instruction_names)) {
+	if (id >= ARR_SIZE(s_instruction_names)) {
 		return NULL;
 	}
 	return s_instruction_names[id];
-- 
2.56.0

